{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e","id":1299621,"title":"Vampire the Requiem 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-25T09:23:08-07:00","id":1299621,"title":"Vampire the Requiem 2e","content":"I purchased many of the VTR books when they were released but never played the system. In the last year or two I've heard about the revised edition and how much of an improvement it is over the original. I'm hesitant to shell out $20 for the PDF when I'm not sure I'd ever run the game but I am curious what these improvements over the original might be and how the game plays differently from how it is written in the original VTR core. Could anyone help me with this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T10:59:03-07:00","id":1299657,"title":"","content":"Whether or not you consider it an improvement depends on what you considered deficient or in need of improvement from first edition. <br /> Personally the only change I unequivocally liked was predator's taint to the predatory aura mechanics. Everything else was changed for the worse or in the case of disciplines simply shifting the problem to a different area. <br /> <br /> Probably the biggest change outside of the game theme shifts is discipline mechanics. Most disciplines require the user to establish a baseline condition from the level 1 power and then work up from there to get higher level effects. The key to resisting most higher level discipline powers is to resist or disable that initial condition because unless it's a handful and a half of other specific rank disciplines, you don't get resist checks for subsequent powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T11:37:20-07:00","id":1299665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1299657#post1299657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most disciplines require the user to establish a baseline condition from the level 1 power and then work up from there to get higher level effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is only the case for two of the ten Disciplines. It is not &quot;most&quot; by any definition of the word.<br /> <br /> Most (though not all) opinions I've seen in this forum, other forums, and reviews is that the Chronicles of Darkness (2e) ruleset is hands-down an improvement over the New World of Darkness (1e) one. Having run both for several years each, I'm inclined to agree. At least for the core materials: I haven't bought a lot of the supplements due to both lack of funds and an apparent steep power creep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T11:51:57-07:00","id":1299669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1299665#post1299665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is only the case for two of the ten Disciplines. It is not &quot;most&quot; by any definition of the word.<br /> <br /> Most (though not all) opinions I've seen in this forum, other forums, and reviews is that the Chronicles of Darkness (2e) ruleset is hands-down an improvement over the New World of Darkness (1e) one. Having run both for several years each, I'm inclined to agree. At least for the core materials: I haven't bought a lot of the supplements due to both lack of funds and an apparent steep power creep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Majesty, Dominate, Nightmare, and Obfuscate require you to have installed a condition using a previous level of the discipline. Only level 5 of Majesty provisionally lets you do an end run around that. And even specific levels of Animalism and Protean require you to use previous levels in order to benefit from higher. That is all the disciplines except Auspex (which arguably doesn't really fit since higher levels are usually more effective once you've gone fishing with the lower levels) and the three physicals. 6 out of 10 is 60% therefore meets the definition of &quot;MOST&quot; disciplines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T12:09:47-07:00","id":1299681,"title":"","content":"You are moving goalposts. You said &quot;Most disciplines require the user to establish a <b>baseline condition</b> from the <b>level 1</b> power and then work up from there to get higher level effects.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is absolutely not the case. Protean does not use Conditions at all. One of the powers enhances an earlier power, but that is neither a level 1 power or a Condition. The same is the case for Obfuscate; no Conditions, only powers that enhance and provide additional functionality to lower level powers. As you admit, the same is true of Animalism. The level 1 Nightmare Discipline doesn't involve Conditions at all, and only the capstone level 5 ability requires Conditions to use. The others get no benefit whatsoever.<br /> <br /> There are only two Disciplines in the game that &quot;establish a baseline condition from the level 1 power and then work up from there.&quot; There are only two Disciplines where &quot;the key to resisting [...] discipline powers is to resist or disable that initial condition.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T12:45:04-07:00","id":1299695,"title":"","content":"I personally prefer 2ed. so far compared to 1ed. And honestly I always felt the same feeling from the most part of the users from this forum.<br /> <br /> I love the new disciplines design. Nightmare and Animalism are now a very good option to go. Physical disciplines are not a waste of px as in the 1ed and much more. <br /> I love the new Frenzy system and Banes are something able to diversificate every kindred giving to the degeneration a deeper and more horrorific meaning.<br /> <br /> There is a lot to talk about and, ultimately, if you are going to like or not the changes it's only depending on your personal tastes but I would for sure recomend to take it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T12:50:58-07:00","id":1299698,"title":"","content":"Would you say the tone of the game remains consistent between the editions. <br /> <br /> From my admittedly limited understanding of Requiem its a game focused less about Machiavellian machinations between vampire elders and instead a game of intense personal horror and night to night survival? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T13:49:47-07:00","id":1299722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1299698#post1299698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you say the tone of the game remains consistent between the editions.<br /> <br /> From my admittedly limited understanding of Requiem its a game focused less about Machiavellian machinations between vampire elders and instead a game of intense personal horror and night to night survival?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue both but we've played both extensively. I'd agree with you that 2nd edition is more about personal horror. You have more things to keep track of in your immediate vicinity. You got your touch stone that basically gives you an excuse/encouragement to continue to interact in some capacity with your former life. Blood Potency also provides more immediate benefits. You can spend 2 vitae a turn at blood potency 2 as opposed to 4 in 1st edition (If I re-call.) this continues for each level you raise. Disciplines are a lot more balanced and as a result feel a lot more powerful. Vampires are more durable. Vampires now downgrade sources of lethal into bashing and most sources of aggravated (there are exceptions) into lethal. So combat is a very different dynamic and a lot less lethal as a result. Two vampires fighting are more likely to beat one into it submits rather than into torpor. Murder would have to be something deliberate and planned for creating more drama in that regard.<br /> <br /> You don't have the frenzy chance upon meeting new vampires. That's been done away with. The covenants are also different and rather than being outright political rivals to each other are more different organizations with different goals. Far more compatible than they used to be. Also now you can take additional banes to stave off the drop in humanity which gives you additional weaknesses (there's examples in the book but you can get creative) that can add further development to your character and also other weaknesses to keep track of or keep hidden. On the other hand more weaknesses to exploit in your rivals who will likely pick up an additional bane or two. While it does have a more personal horror feel to it there's no reason why you couldn't use the updated mechanics and run it the way you have been for years.<br /> <br /> Machiavellian scheming is most definitely still a thing. Vampires are paranoid about their banes being discovered, their touch stones being discovered/targeted, and the blood bond is easier to place on each other as well and has less methods of getting around now. You have more reasons not to let others get too close or they might learn additional ways to get to you but I guess that also adds more to that personal horror.<br /> <br /> If I'm wrong on things I don't mind others correcting me. It's been awhile now since I played 1st edition but those are some of the main differences that come to mind.<br /> <br /> *Edit* In short my advice is look up what the disciplines do now and if you're not interested in the idea of banes, touch stones, more durable vampires, and loss of the predator aura (in the sense of vampires being on edge meeting each other), and many of the other changes.. you might be just fine keeping what you have. If the new stuff sounds interesting you might want to give it a shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25183-reslin","name":"Reslin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25183_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T14:30:51-07:00","id":1299733,"title":"","content":"I'd say if you buy anything, get the 2e corebook (or the God-Machine Update, which is basically a patch document for the 1e corebook). The most dramatic improvements are there: revised experience system, new rules for chases and social maneuvering, Horrors, etc. The changes to Vampire itself are fairly minor by comparison\u2014the themes stayed mostly the same, and most of the ideas from 1e (five clans, five covenants, ten disciplines) are the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T16:42:26-07:00","id":1299771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1299698#post1299698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you say the tone of the game remains consistent between the editions. <br /> <br /> From my admittedly limited understanding of Requiem its a game focused less about Machiavellian machinations between vampire elders and instead a game of intense personal horror and night to night survival? <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The tone is pretty much the same. Soemthing good of Requiem in general is that it allows you to give the taint you prefer or any mix. <br /> <br /> You have plenty of personal horror hooks: Banes, Frenzy, ecc.<br /> But also very intricated politics: several Covenants fighting each other more or less openly, almost the same feudal hierarchy and so on. <br /> Something I forgot and I really love about 2 ed (Draconis already cited them) ate the new chases and Social manouvres system. <br /> I think that if properly used they add to a normal chase a lot more variety, pushing both the player and Master to be creative and original. Same for the social manouvres, even though they can' be used for anything but just in special occasions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T23:21:15-07:00","id":1299868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1299698#post1299698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you say the tone of the game remains consistent between the editions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Short answer, yes, long answer, mostly. If you dig back into the really early Requiem supplements the tone is a bit different. It's coming fresh off Masquerade and doesn't want to rock the boat too much, but it's also trying hard <i>not </i>to just be Masquerade 2.0, so much of the oldest material is stuck between those two impulses. Once you hit Damnation City and Requiem for Rome (which was kind of a soft reboot of the line anyway), the difference between first edition and second edition is more academic, apart from rules. I'd argue there are bigger tonal changes <i>within </i>the first edition than between first and second.<br /> <br /> As for improvements, I think the biggest is the Disciplines. The 2E Disciplines might contain the best version of those powers in any version of <b>Vampire</b>. They really dig into the power fantasy <i>and</i> the horror of being one of the Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T23:34:26-07:00","id":1299871,"title":"","content":"Rose Bailey has said a few times that VtR 2e unofficially started well before 2e was even going to be a thing, as the last few years of VtR supplements were all designed by the principles that lead to VtR 2e's approach.<br /> <br /> One thing that I think is important to explain about the Disciplines is that they actually make sense as 1-5 rated powers. They're not a collection of powers around a theme forced into the idea of needing each dot to be a better power than the ones before it. They actually feel like a cohesive study of a vampire power that grows in applications over time. That's why there's a lot of internal synergy where higher powers use earlier powers in some way. You don't just get a new Dominate power that falls under the themes of Dominate, you get better at Dominate itself.<br /> <br /> Another small change that has a big tonal emphasis behind it? All of the Banes (universal like sun light, Clan, and ones you pick up to protect Humanity) are all keyed off of Humanity. This really sells the idea that being a vampire kicks ass and is awesome... at first. As your start to drop those first few dots of Humanity, you start getting kicked harder by Banes and it turns out that the Embrace wasn't what it seemed like at first. High Humanity is, paradoxically, it's own form of power for vampires that can keep it up, since it means they can avoid the perils other vampires face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T23:42:37-07:00","id":1299872,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna take a second to disagree with everyone on the tone, using words from when it Blood and Smoke first came out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Truth be told, if I had to pick the one reason I never liked Requiem, it was it's tone. It was just a little too deep in it's own tragedy.<br /> <br /> Blood and Smoke is clever, sexy, and stylish. The tragedy is still there, in the subtext. But it's all delivered with smooth smiles, confident strides, celebratory grotesqueness, and blood-stained cool. </div> </div> </div>This is a very true thing. Requiem First was openly deep in the bleak for tone. Requiem Second is more playful, more devil-may-care, and and coyly &quot;in denial&quot; on just how close the bleak really is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T12:40:30-07:00","id":1300038,"title":"","content":"I'm going to be a bit negative here and say that I didn't really like with 2nd edition was, and I claim no special expertise at all on the subject, was that it was more rules. I like the old systems because there were not as many rules to keep track of as in many other systems and the die system was easy. Just roll a number of d10 and count successes. Simple. To me who likes it rules light the new rules got a bit more than what I had wanted. But then again I've only checked through the book so feel free to totally ignore me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T12:47:27-07:00","id":1300041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1300038#post1300038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to be a bit negative here and say that I didn't really like with 2nd edition was, and I claim no special expertise at all on the subject, was that it was more rules. I like the old systems because there were not as many rules to keep track of as in many other systems and the die system was easy. Just roll a number of d10 and count successes. Simple. To me who likes it rules light the new rules got a bit more than what I had wanted. But then again I've only checked through the book so feel free to totally ignore me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty vague. It's not like 2e has stepped away from the basic mechanism of rolling dice and counting successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T13:03:39-07:00","id":1300048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1300041#post1300041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is pretty vague. It's not like 2e has stepped away from the basic mechanism of rolling dice and counting successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its very true, because I don't have extensive experience with the system and I &quot;learn by doing&quot; so to say. I hoped I made it clear in my post that this is a rather loose opinion and not a post of great authority and insight. And everyone should feel free to ignore it.<br /> <br /> But the thing that I disliked was that some new rules, like for example touchstones, were added. I felt that the Humanity system worked well enough as it did and I really liked the slim approach to rules that 1st edition did have. I really dislike going back to &quot;Mask and Dirge&quot; archetypes like the &quot;Demeanor and Nature&quot; from the old VtM. I feel that these complicates the game rather than adding to it. Or at least my experience is that the &quot;Virtue and Vice&quot; system was easier to understand and manage and lent itself better to the games I could and wanted to run.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T14:12:24-07:00","id":1300086,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, 2e is a vast improvement over 1e.<br /> <br /> A couple of the (in my opinion) most important improvements:<br /> <br /> 1. The theme of 1e was that it sucks to be a vampire, and you just have to deal with it. The theme of 2e is that being a vampire is not fun, but it isn't without its perks either. You're a monster now, but you're a bad ass monster. You can actually kick some serious ass straight out of the gate, even as a fledgling turned yesterday. In 2e, you get abilities like Lashing Out with your predatory aura, buffing your physical capabilities with Physical Intensity and you're immediately an amazing blood hound with your new and improved Kindred Senses. You also downgrade <i>all</i> mundane damage to bashing damage now, making you a lot more durable than you were as a human, even in a knife fight. Finally, your first dot Discipline abilities are a lot stronger in 2e and they're all free to use, they don't cost you any Vitae, so you can immediately bully the humans around you with your new Discipline powers, without having to worry that you're going to grow hungry.<br /> So yeah, being a new vampire is still not great, but it doesn't suck outright, and you're actually a scary monster straight out of the gate, so that's a huge improvement over 1e.<br /> <br /> 2. The Humanity system is a lot more elegant in 2e. It isn't a glorified morality system anymore, but it now actually does what it's supposed to do: tracking your humanity (I know, wild, right?). Committing mass murder is still a Breaking Point, but not because murder is bad and you should feel bad, but because murder feeds the inner Beast, makes it grow stronger, makes it crawl to the surface. Monstrous acts are Breaking Points, but circumstances that remind you of how much of a monster you really are, are Breaking Points as well in 2e. Spending a few hours in the sun (yes, that's possible in 2e if you're young and have high Humanity) is a Breaking Point. Surviving something that should have killed you if you were human, is a Breaking Point. Going without human contact for more than a week, is a Breaking Point. These are all things that remind you that you aren't human anymore, and thus they are Humanity Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> 3. Touchstones are the best new addition in 2e. I love the whole concept of it. Touchstones are things that keeps your vampire character connected to his human side, to keep the Beast at bay. This Touchstone often comes in the form of a human character your vampire cares about. It forces players to anchor their vampire characters in human society (or suffer the consequences of not doing so), it forces the vampire characters to interact with humanity, which in turn leads to good dramatic scenes and paints a clear picture of how being a vampire sets you apart from the rest of humanity. It keeps the game grounded and it reminds the players of how monstrous their characters really are. Imagine your vampire accidentally murdered his meal last night during a hunger frenzy, and then when he visits his Touchstone, he has to listen to her crying about receiving the news that some sick psychopath assaulted and murdered her boyfriend last night. It puts things in perspective.<br /> <br /> 4. Conditions. This has replaced the Derangements from 1e. It's much better. Instead of being (semi)permanent, they are temporary nerfs and boons, often coming in the form of a dice penalty or bonus, which affects your character in certain fields, and can be resolved in certain ways, granting your character a Beat (the new way of tracking character progression in 2e). It's more flexible, it feels more organic, it might seem a little game-y at first and perhaps it is, but it's game-y in a good way. The Condition encourages good dramatic roleplaying from the players, by giving the players penalties and buffs, and rewarding them with Beats if the player roleplays the Condition in an interesting way.<br /> The new vampire Disciplines are also tied into this Condition system, as others before me mentioned. Using Dominate for example, applies the Mesmerized Condition to the target, which means the target is subject to your will, and can be commanded for the duration of the scene. However, the Mesmerized Condition is resolved when the target experiences a Breaking Point, or if the target suffers damage, which means your grip over her slips. This means you have to be tactical about how you use your Dominate. Yes, Dominate is more powerful in 2e, but the target also has more ways to break free if you aren't careful. It all feels so much more organic, dynamic and interesting than 1e did without the Conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 03-26-2019, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T03:51:24-07:00","id":1300228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1300038#post1300038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to be a bit negative here and say that I didn't really like with 2nd edition was, and I claim no special expertise at all on the subject, was that it was more rules. I like the old systems because there were not as many rules to keep track of as in many other systems and the die system was easy. Just roll a number of d10 and count successes. Simple. To me who likes it rules light the new rules got a bit more than what I had wanted. But then again I've only checked through the book so feel free to totally ignore me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I do not get you here. The rule systemn is more or less the same. Conditions have repleaced Derangements and while they could seems more compley at first, they actually really help the player and the Master to keep track about the effect of any .... &quot;condition&quot; they have. Wether it be applied through mundane circumstances or Supernatural powers. It also help to intepret them.<br /> <br /> Except for that the dice system is pretty much the same, with a more well designed discipline system. <br /> <br /> Touchstone is something you could also ignore. Just do not have the bonus it gives to you, but the idea is quite good as it is something that keep you &quot;on earth&quot;. And when you are going to loose the Touchstone bound because any degeneration, it also provide you very good interpretation hooks (at least in my personal experience).<br /> <br /> Mask and Dirge workd pretty wells and do not need to be confudes with Nature and Demeanor as they means something different: Mask is how you do mask your Mosntrous nature to the Kins, Dirge is how you approach yopurself to Kindred. This is good because it &quot;push&quot; you to interpret and characterize better the beahviour of your PC as it's the only way to regain WP. And still this not bound your PC to only this as it is not intended as representing your very &quot;nature&quot;. I see Dirge as another possiible MASK used between Kindred. Having Dirge: Authoritarian does not mean that, when alone, you couldn't feel yourself a nurturer indeed.<br /> <br /> So I really see 2ed a huge improvment on 1ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T12:38:01-07:00","id":1300360,"title":"","content":"I will just say that I really didn't expect this much response to my post. But I will admit that I don't want an edition war and I've said what I wanted to say, so will say no more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T16:18:31-07:00","id":1300410,"title":"","content":"It was certainly not my intention to start an edition war either. But the OP asked what 2e has to offer, so I gave the 4 (in my opinion) best things 2e has to offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:07:18-07:00","id":1301400,"title":"","content":"Meh, I have mixed feelings on the mechanical changes of 2e but I did NOT like the setting changes of 2e, namely removing both Belial's Brood and the Fog of Ages and the increased emphasis on the Strix.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the Strix are one of the worst and most unnecessary antagonists in the entire Chronicles of Darkness lineup. At least in my opinion.<br /> <br /> If you want the 2e mechanics, then go for 2e but maybe get some of the 1e books and use elements from 1e's setting, such as Belial's Brood and the more mysterious version of VII from the early days of Requiem. Avoid the Strix at all costs unless you want your game derailed by invincible and all-powerful owl ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:31:27-07:00","id":1301405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301400#post1301400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">namely removing both Belial's Brood</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/belials-brood-night-horrors-spilled-blood/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/belials-brood-night-horrors-spilled-blood/\" target=\"_blank\"> Belial&rsquo;s Brood [Night Horrors: Spilled Blood] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/belials-brood-night-horrors-spilled-blood/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/belials-brood-night-horrors-spilled-blood/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:31:37-07:00","id":1301406,"title":"","content":"Belial's brood do still exist, but didn't make the page count cut. The new 2e books spilled blood (I think that's the name?) Is set to have Belial's brood make a comeback in a big way. <br /> <br /> The fog of ages thing is a little decisive, I feel 2e's core did not do a great job explaining the changes but 1k years of night did. The big change is that vampires don't have supernatural memory (without the right merits) so most elders just.. forget stuff happened. Essentially the idea, from my reading, is to to provide more opportunities. Under the new system you can either have a elder forget everything becuse it's been 200 years, or you can have them remember and get caught up in century long schemes and conspiracies that don't work if vampires forget everything all when they torpor. <br /> <br /> Strix - great antagonist, for my hunter games. Strix seems to be hit or miss, but really they are not that core to the game so just ignoring them doesn't really change the game at all. I like them, but I get why people wouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:33:48-07:00","id":1301409,"title":"","content":"1) The Belial's Brood are not removed, they were just simply not included in the core book and, in fact, are coming out in the next book.<br /> 2) You don't like the Strix, don't use them. Nothing forces you to.<br /> 3) Seriously, the worst and most unnecessary antagonist in the entire Chronicles lineup? With a whole extensive canon out there, I have my doubts on this. Changing Breeds has worse antagonists at a sneeze by virtue of some of the charachter types just always being available as antagonists, and I came up with that on a yawn.<br /> 4) By the way-look man, a lot of us are old hands at your arguments, but others are not, so just <i>insisting</i> that the Strix are the worst without elaboration is horse shit. Either present the reasons for your opinion or hold it back.<br /> 5) I've got nothing about the Fog of Ages except that I personally don't care-I can think of reasons for or against and can run or not run the Fog in my games at a whim.<br /> <br /> Would it kill you to please just think about how you present yourself, for, like, a minute?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:49:46-07:00","id":1301414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301409#post1301409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) The Belial's Brood are not removed, they were just simply not included in the core book and, in fact, are coming out in the next book.<br /> 2) You don't like the Strix, don't use them. Nothing forces you to.<br /> 3) Seriously, the worst and most unnecessary antagonist in the entire Chronicles lineup? With a whole extensive canon out there, I have my doubts on this. Changing Breeds has worse antagonists at a sneeze by virtue of some of the charachter types just always being available as antagonists, and I came up with that on a yawn.<br /> 4) By the way-look man, a lot of us are old hands at your arguments, but others are not, so just <i>insisting</i> that the Strix are the worst without elaboration is horse shit. Either present the reasons for your opinion or hold it back.<br /> 5) I've got nothing about the Fog of Ages except that I personally don't care-I can think of reasons for or against and can run or not run the Fog in my games at a whim.<br /> <br /> Would it kill you to please just think about how you present yourself, for, like, a minute?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright, you want me to explain why I think the Strix are a terrible antagonist (not counting playable character templates such as the aforementioned Changing Breeds), I can do that...<br /> <br /> 1. They're invincible super-villains that went from a simple plot device in Requiem for Rome to the main antagonist of the entire Requiem line in 2e that are somehow responsible or connected to every single event in Kindred history and society, despite having no real motive or personality on account of being freakin' birds.<b> I am exaggerating here, </b>but not by much.<br /> <br /> 2. Even though they are technically optional, a Requiem ST who wants to play without the Strix in their game while still incorporating the game's backstory will have a hard time unless they do like me and Rule Zero the fuck out of the game<br /> <br /> 3. As a threat to vampires, they're kind of redundant. Kindred already have plenty to fear such as fire, sunlight, hunters, the cops, other denizens of the setting such as werewolves and mages, and most of all, other vampires. No need to include super-powered ghost birds that cannot be stopped and have no real motive for their actions whatsoever.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, I am glad that Belial's Brood is finally coming back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 03-31-2019, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:55:54-07:00","id":1301415,"title":"","content":"Have we read the same book? Strix are side-mentioned in a few optional backstories, they're not integral to the backstory. You know how easy it is not to have Strix? Just don't include them. There's no giant gaping holes that now need to be filled. <br /> <br /> Secondly, they're not invincible, just tough. They're not connected to every single event in Kindred history or society, they're connected to Requiem for Rome, and 2-3 other single lines that you can describe. That, to my knowledge, is pretty much it. <br /> <br /> So I'mma just say &quot;that's a lie&quot; and you can cite page numbers if you want to defend yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:59:26-07:00","id":1301417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301400#post1301400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, I have mixed feelings on the mechanical changes of 2e but I did NOT like the setting changes of 2e, namely removing both Belial's Brood and the Fog of Ages and the increased emphasis on the Strix.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the Strix are one of the worst and most unnecessary antagonists in the entire Chronicles of Darkness lineup. At least in my opinion.<br /> <br /> If you want the 2e mechanics, then go for 2e but maybe get some of the 1e books and use elements from 1e's setting, such as Belial's Brood and the more mysterious version of VII from the early days of Requiem. Avoid the Strix at all costs unless you want your game derailed by invincible and all-powerful owl ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>As many have said both VII and Belial are still a thing.<br /> Fog of mist are something I've disliked a lot in 1ed actually. Glad to not have it anymore. <br /> I don't like strix too much as well but I've just used once and it wasn't so bad. More over if you do not use them the theme won't change. It's not a reason to not play with 2ed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:00:02-07:00","id":1301418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301415#post1301415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have we read the same book? Strix are side-mentioned in a few optional backstories, they're not integral to the backstory. You know how easy it is not to have Strix? Just don't include them. There's no giant gaping holes that now need to be filled.<br /> <br /> Secondly, they're not invincible, just tough. They're not connected to every single event in Kindred history or society, they're connected to Requiem for Rome, and 2-3 other single lines that you can describe. That, to my knowledge, is pretty much it.<br /> <br /> So I'mma just say &quot;that's a lie&quot; and you can cite page numbers if you want to defend yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is a difference between a lie and hyperbole. I even said that I was exaggerating in my post.<br /> <br /> I know I don't have to include them and I don't, but the fact that they got a whole chapter to themselves in 2e, regardless of how self-contained it may be is just disappointing.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if I were in charge of Requiem 2E, I would not have included the Strix at all in the corebook and instead saved them for another supplement like they did with Belial's Brood or put them in a 2E update of Requiem For Rome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 03-31-2019, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:15:12-07:00","id":1301423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301414#post1301414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Alright, you want me to explain why I think the Strix are a terrible antagonist (not counting playable character templates such as the aforementioned Changing Breeds), I can do that...<br /> <br /> 1. They're invincible super-villains that went from a simple plot device in Requiem for Rome to the main antagonist of the entire Requiem line in 2e that are somehow responsible or connected to every single event in Kindred history and society, despite having no real motive or personality on account of being freakin' birds.<b> I am exaggerating here, </b>but not by much.<br /> <br /> 2. Even though they are technically optional, a Requiem ST who wants to play without the Strix in their game while still incorporating the game's backstory will have a hard time unless they do like me and Rule Zero the fuck out of the game<br /> <br /> 3. As a threat to vampires, they're kind of redundant. Kindred already have plenty to fear such as fire, sunlight, hunters, the cops, other denizens of the setting such as werewolves and mages, and most of all, other vampires. No need to include super-powered ghost birds that cannot be stopped and have no real motive for their actions whatsoever.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, I am glad that Belial's Brood is finally coming back.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. That's a complete lie...... Have you ever faced them? They are good threats but not invicible at all....<br /> 2. jus....why???? Actually they've been much more crucial in 1ed with requiem for Rome...they where responsible of Juli fall. I gues you miss info.<br /> 3. What's the point to citate as a threat banes and antagonist togheter, while werewolves are not anymore natural enemies. Really seems to me you are talking just because you are fanatically against strix. You've also citated cops............less then puppets in kindred hands. Anyone can be an antagonist, Strix are just another kind....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:26:17-07:00","id":1301428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301423#post1301423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1. That's a complete lie...... Have you ever faced them? They are good threats but not invicible at all....<br /> 2. jus....why???? Actually they've been much more crucial in 1ed with requiem for Rome...they where responsible of Juli fall. I gues you miss info.<br /> 3. What's the point to citate as a threat banes and antagonist togheter, while werewolves are not anymore natural enemies. Really seems to me you are talking just because you are fanatically against strix. You've also citated cops............less then puppets in kindred hands. Anyone can be an antagonist, Strix are just another kind....</div> </div> </div> </div>I know werewolves aren't natural enemies of vampires like they were in Masquerade, but what I am saying is that they have better potential as an enemy or hazard to the Kindred than the Strix.<br /> <br /> Again, this is just my opinion and nothing more so feel free to disagree with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 03-31-2019, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:50:44-07:00","id":1301438,"title":"","content":"What are you-<br /> <br /> <i>I literally ran a twelve week game without a Strix appearing <b><u>once.</u></b> I commented on them for a total number of <b><u>zero.</u></b></i><br /> <br /> Dude, you don't like them, fine, but don't try to bullshit me about how fucking integral the Strix are now, because I have <i>god damn </i><i>experience</i> that says otherwise, and that's without accounting for the fact that <i>this kind of shit is my side-job</i>.<br /> <br /> Seriously dude, I don't think you actually play these games. I literally don't believe you have ever tried. I don't think you even know what it's like to play at a table. Feel free to prove me wrong! But at this literal instant, I <i>do not believe you</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:05:21-07:00","id":1301442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301428#post1301428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this is just my opinion and nothing more so feel free to disagree with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is you continually present your opinions as facts in attempts to back them up. You rail against things that don't match your tastes to try to make it sound like they're objectively bad, and you complain endlessly about how much people post bad things about what you like.<br /> <br /> For the love of whatever will get you to stop?<br /> <br /> Fucking stop already. You can dislike the Strix without lying about them; and trying to hide lies beneath 'exaggeration' is low even for you. What you would do if you were in charge of the game doesn't really matter, because nobody would ever let you be in charge of a WoD or CofD game, because you don't want to make these games, you want to make similar games that are more to your taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:10:19-07:00","id":1301446,"title":"","content":"'I can see people disagree with me so I'm going to bow out of this, I'm sorry I won't do it again until I do.'<br /> <br /> Rather than re-iterating your dislikes, maybe get a blog and just link to it in your signature. If people are interested in what you have to say, they can go to your blog and you don't have to keep posting then backing out of these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:12:04-07:00","id":1301448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301442#post1301442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is you continually present your opinions as facts in attempts to back them up. You rail against things that don't match your tastes to try to make it sound like they're objectively bad, and you complain endlessly about how much people post bad things about what you like.<br /> <br /> For the love of whatever will get you to stop?<br /> <br /> Fucking stop already. You can dislike the Strix without lying about them; and trying to hide lies beneath 'exaggeration' is low even for you. What you would do if you were in charge of the game doesn't really matter, because nobody would ever let you be in charge of a WoD or CofD game, because you don't want to make these games, you want to make similar games that are more to your taste.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I never tried to present anything as fact but whatever makes you feel good I suppose. If making me into a strawman villain will make you feel better, so be it.<br /> <br /> All I was saying is that if someone was interested in 2e Requiem, they should also get some 1e books for context and compare the settings before deciding which one they prefer (with the caveat that I personally dislike the 2e setting changes because of the Strix) and maybe I wasn't the best at wording it but then again. I am an idiot.<br /> <br /> Look, I have considered giving Requiem 2e's mechanics a chance and I am not as militantly opposed to 2e as I was in the past, and in fact, if I ever was going to use the Humanity mechanic, I would choose 2e's Humanity system over 1e's any day of the week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:29:19-07:00","id":1301453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301446#post1301446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'I can see people disagree with me so I'm going to bow out of this, I'm sorry I won't do it again until I do.'<br /> <br /> Rather than re-iterating your dislikes, maybe get a blog and just link to it in your signature. If people are interested in what you have to say, they can go to your blog and you don't have to keep posting then backing out of these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a great idea.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> You think I don't play these games and never have? I'll admit, I have more experience with VTM LARP than I ever did with VTR tabletop but I do own the Requiem 1E books and if you sincerely want me to prove you wrong, I can.<br /> <br /> Hell, I will even invite you to a game and show you how it's done if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:36:15-07:00","id":1301455,"title":"","content":"Dude, I <i>seriously</i> have to ask:<br /> <br /> What do you <i>expect</i> to happen when you do this? <i>How</i> does this play out in your head when you're sitting there, tapping away at your keyboard?<br /> <br /> Again, <i>ten years of this</i>. At this point, I would love either to know what goes through your head when you make posts or would love you to <i>just </i>stop.<br /> <br /> I would also love for you to finally learn the lessons laid out at your feet, but I am <i>really not holding my breath for that</i>. So that pretty much leaves me with wondering what the hell you think is/was/will happen/ing when you do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:39:14-07:00","id":1301457,"title":"","content":"The above would also make me happy compared to the standard Camilla isn't ready to leave for now passive aggressive snap responses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:46:10-07:00","id":1301463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301455#post1301455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, I <i>seriously</i> have to ask:<br /> <br /> What do you <i>expect</i> to happen when you do this? <i>How</i> does this play out in your head when you're sitting there, tapping away at your keyboard?<br /> <br /> Again, <i>ten years of this</i>. At this point, I would love either to know what goes through your head when you make posts or would love you to <i>just </i>stop.<br /> <br /> I would also love for you to finally learn the lessons laid out at your feet, but I am <i>really not holding my breath for that</i>. So that pretty much leaves me with wondering what the hell you think is/was/will happen/ing when you do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know and expect that I am going to get backlash for having the &quot;wrong&quot; opinions, and to be honest, I deserve the backlash because regardless of how valid my opinions are, I really fucking hate myself. No joke here, I'm serious.<br /> <br /> Honestly, a lot of it is fueled by self-hatred and the fact that I am a scumbag who deserves to be punished for a lot of shit (most of which happened off-site) and I neither want nor deserve pity for it.<br /> <br /> I hate myself and part of me wants to die, but I am too chickenshit to physically harm myself so I harm myself psychologically and emotionally as a form of penance and atonement for past misdeeds, both online and in real life.<br /> <br /> I do want to one day run my own Requiem game either at a table or online, but I also feel as if I don't deserve to so I don't. Most of my WoD experiences is Classic WoD LARP.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help that most of the people in my IRL gaming space either hate White Wolf completely or hate Requiem because it replaced Masquerade, and I don't seek online gaming all that much because a lot of online Requiem games are either angst-fests or nobody's interested in what I like anyway, and even if they were, I don't think I'd be intelligent or good enough to run a successful Requiem game or Lost game, or anything really.<br /> <br /> (Before anyone jumps my ass, I am NOT suicide-baiting. As I said earlier in the post, I'm too much of a chickenshit loser to actually go through with something like that, I'm just extremely depressed all the time and full of guilt and shame over a lot of things in my life)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 03-31-2019, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T16:07:47-07:00","id":1301739,"title":"","content":"My dude, you need help, not a forum or a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T16:35:24-07:00","id":1301741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301428#post1301428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know werewolves aren't natural enemies of vampires like they were in Masquerade, but what I am saying is that they have better potential as an enemy or hazard to the Kindred than the Strix.<br /> <br /> Again, this is just my opinion and nothing more so feel free to disagree with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I'm just curious why do you think werewolves make a better antagonist than Strix? At least how they're presented in nWoD/CofD werewolves are all about interacting with Shadow spirits and vampires absolutely do <i>not</i>, and, obviously, Strix are specifically designed to harry vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T16:59:47-07:00","id":1301751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301741#post1301741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm just curious why do you think werewolves make a better antagonist than Strix? At least how they're presented in nWoD/CofD werewolves are all about interacting with Shadow spirits and vampires absolutely do <i>not</i>, and, obviously, Strix are specifically designed to harry vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just don't like the Strix and I find the concept of spooky ghost owls with no real motives of any kind to be a lame antagonist in general.<br /> <br /> Even if werewolves in CofD have nothing to do with vampires, there's more potential in them as antagonists in my opinion than there are in the Strix, who I find to be very shallow and one-dimensional (and that's sad when I am the one saying such things)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301739#post1301739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My dude, you need help, not a forum or a game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No argument from me there. But while I probably do need help, I'm honestly not sure if I deserve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 04-01-2019, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T18:30:30-07:00","id":1301772,"title":"","content":"Good thing that the Strix aren't a lame atangonist because they lack real motives. I'm glad I read the books before judging things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T18:45:26-07:00","id":1301774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301772#post1301772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good thing that the Strix aren't a lame atangonist because they lack real motives. I'm glad I read the books before judging things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even if you do like the Strix, I don't.<br /> <br /> So don't force me to use them if I don't want to. If you want Strix in your games, that's fine. But I don't.<br /> <br /> Why do you even care what I think? Is my opinion worth that much to you? It's not even worth that much to me.<br /> <br /> Either way, I will write a blog to contain these opinions of mine, it will make things easier for both of us. You guys are annoyed with me (and rightfully so) and I intellectually know that punishing myself like this is not healthy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 04-01-2019, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T20:42:27-07:00","id":1301799,"title":"","content":"I'm pointing out that the 'lack real motives' critique is bullshit. You can love them, hate them, or be completely ambivalent towards the Strix without misrepresenting them.<br /> <br /> People still here for the point of the thread to think about if they want to consider VtR 2e deserve a real discussion of things, not just mud flinging.<br /> <br /> There's actually some decent critiques of how the Strix motivations are structured. Their general motivations as a group could use a paragraph or so to give them a bit more teeth. The &quot;jealous of living things since they'll never be a living thing,&quot; aspect is a good motivation for why they're so active in attacking people and causing trouble compared to other ephemeral entities (and even why they care so much about the undead as the closest they can get to being alive), but there's a bit of a lacking in a why they care. Though they're NPC only baddies and STs don't really need more depth to be able to portray them well.<br /> <br /> Also, Strix are highly individualistic and hugely defined by their Vice (since they lack the diversity of character traits and anchors like most characters). The areas of vagueness in their general motivations as antagonists are largely there because they're not all going to approach it the same way. Overly defining the why of their envy of the living reduces the variations on individual Strix.<br /> <br /> To relate this back to that werewolf thing. Apocalypse werewolves really only worked as antagonists for vampires in two arenas: direct violent enemies, or cagey allies of another faction working with some vampires against a greater good and helping eliminate vampires not on board. Forsaken werewolves have nearly countless ways they might come into conflict with vampires, as there's nothing predetermined in them coming into conflict at all. Each instance is going to be somewhat unique even if we could create some basic categories of them.<br /> <br /> The Strix are far more like Forskaen than Apocalypse; even if a bit in the middle. While they have innate reasons to be in conflict with vampires, each Strix has their own interpretations on why, and how they want to handle it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T21:33:40-07:00","id":1301808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301774#post1301774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So don't force me to use them if I don't want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody here is doing so or even <i>capable of</i> doing so, but\u2026<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do you even care what I think? </div> </div> </div><i>\u2026you keep coming into threads and sharing your thoughts in the inflammatory manner of lies and exaggeration.</i><br /> <br /> Nobody especially gives a shit <i>what</i> your opinion is about these games, but you've been a particularly outspoken nuisance about it for literal years and have consistently provided powerful evidence against the idea that you've been listening meaningfully to what people have been telling you, apparently now as part of some ill-considered form of self-flaggelation that none of us signed up for.<br /> <br /> Closing your eyes and covering your ears when people tell you that the superficial claims you've layered over the perfectly understandable sentiment of &quot;eh, I just don't like it and I'm not really invested in trying to like it&quot; are bad arguments doesn't make you an &quot;iconoclast.&quot; This is <i>below</i> rebel-without-a-cause. This is some <i>Don Quixote</i> shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T21:40:56-07:00","id":1301809,"title":"","content":"I'll get back around to the other stuff, but I want to take a note while, disturbing as the self evisceration was Cam, it didn't actually answer the question I originally posed. It's kind of a dodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T05:31:17-07:00","id":1301866,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I'll add my two cents on the strix and how I'd advice to run them. I'm not sure if it will change <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a> 's mind, but hopefully this will be useful for someone who reads this:<br /> <br /> The strix, I feel, are the types of antagonists best handled as singular entities. When I look at the example strix NPCs in the core 2e book, I notice there is almost nothing they have in common, other than a universal hatred for Humanity (with an upper case 'H', though I'm sure they hate humanity as well, but specifically for what makes us humane). But look at each individual strix NPC, and you will see a whole bunch of additional motivations that drive this individual strix, motivations that are not necessarily shared by the rest of its kind, but still motivations that will set events in motions and cause entire chronicles to happen.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> pointed out, the strix seem to be motivated by their Vice. One could even argue that they <i>are</i> their Vice. But how that Vice manifests itself and how it drives the strix, is different for each individual strix.<br /> <br /> Anna Red, for example, embodies Wrath by brutally slaughtering humans in very Ripper-esque ways, for no other reason than to torment entire boroughs, human and vampire alike. It's not just her wrath we're talking about here either, but the wrath she inspires into the people of the city or borough she plagues. There is a certain methodology to her actions and she constantly makes a fool out of the police and Kindred she eludes. The general population becomes angry at the police for their perceived incompetence. The police becomes angry at the journalists who's publications on the serial killer cause outrage, people all across the city shout &quot;conspiracy!&quot; and &quot;cover-up!&quot;, the Irish are certain the killer is a Jew, the Jews blame the gypsies and the gypsies blame the Irish. And the vampires? They're at each other's throat in much the same way. Simply put, when Anne Red is doing her work, the people around her will start to embody fear at first, but it will quickly turn into anger, rage, wrath.<br /> <br /> Mother, on the other hand, she is without purpose and she knows that, which bothers her to no end. So she gave herself a purpose, a very ambitious one. She wants to create a new vampire clan. She knows the strix of old created the Julii, and that is just the most recent example. The other clans were likely created by her cousins as well. Perhaps Mother herself once took part in the creation of a vampire clan, but has lost her way. Even she doesn't know for sure, but what she does know for sure, is that she will rekindle her old purpose and create a new vampire clan... tonight. The fact that so far every attempt resulted in the creation of utter abominations and multiple masquerade breaches, well, that is but a small price to pay for her ambition. In the same way, the monsters she spawns are ambitious themselves, deciding to take the Kindred head on in an all-out turf war. If it isn't obvious already, Mother's Vice is Ambition.<br /> <br /> The way I handle the strix in my chronicle, is that I give each individual strix an entire story arc to himself. I will look at the Vice the strix individual embodies and what his modus operandi is, and then build an entire story with that particular Vice becoming the central theme of the story.<br /> During the majority of the story's chapters, the players will never interact with the strix. They will only deal with the fallout instead. They will feel the ripples the strix is causing, and go on an investigation to figure out what is going on. At this point, the players don't even know they're dealing with a strix yet (because not all my stories revolve around a strix, just some of them).<br /> When the players made some good progress on their investigation, they might draw the attention of the strix, and get to interact with him. The strix will appear in the body of a player's friend, colleague, rival or enemy, with the players being none the wiser.<br /> After this point, it's fine if the players find out that they're dealing with a strix. In fact, you want them to find out, because if you played your cards right, the players who know a bit about how the strix operate (possessing vampires and humans alike), will become immensely paranoid. They will no longer know who to trust, and that is a truly horrific feeling.<br /> While all this is happening, I also try to have the players experience and deal with the Vice the strix embodies. If they're dealing with Anna Red, I want my player's characters to experience wrath, if they are up against Mother, I want to have them deal with ambition, etc. This is not necessary for a good strix story, but I think it's cool.<br /> Eventually the players will either defeat the strix by thwarting the strix's modus operandi, by chasing it off, making it flee the city, or by actually killing it. This victory should never come easy and always come with a feeling of dread. Perhaps the player characters had to kill their best friend to stop this strix. Perhaps the players did something far more monstrous to stop this strix. The player characters should be asking themselves whether the victory was worth their sacrifices. For example, if the players acted extra wrathful when dealing with Anna Red, have them reflect on that, throw in a hint that they aren't necessarily that much better than the monster they just defeated.<br /> Sure, you could end your story on a more positive note if you prefer (and I won't be able to stop you if you do), but come on, this is the Chronicles of <i>Darkness</i>, this is Vampire the Requiem, a game where you play as blood sucking monsters, and monsters don't deserve a happy end, do they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-02-2019, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T09:17:30-07:00","id":1301924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1299621-vampire-the-requiem-2e?p=1301866#post1301866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, you could end your story on a more positive note if you prefer (and I won't be able to stop you if you do), but come on, this is the Chronicles of <i>Darkness</i>, this is Vampire the Requiem, a game where you play as blood sucking monsters, and monsters don't deserve a happy end, do they?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna save time and just point out that this is definitely not Cam's jam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T10:00:05-07:00","id":1301937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div cl